# graphify-out/ is 100% derived from source — nothing in it is hand-edited. It used to be
# committed deliberately so both of us shared one graph, but a shared *generated* directory
# means every independent local rebuild is a guaranteed future conflict: it corrupted itself
# with raw `<<<<<<<` markers twice in one evening once GitDoc started auto-syncing, once badly
# enough to spill into real source (TemplateInteractiveSandbox.tsx got merge-mangled along
# with it). Untracked, it can never appear in a merge at all — same treatment as node_modules/
# or dist/. Each of us just runs `graphify update .` locally whenever we want a current graph.
graphify-out/

# Claude instruction files — untracked on purpose, same reasoning as graphify-out/ above.
# These are rewritten almost every working session (they are where working rules and
# token-saving conventions get tuned), and with GitDoc auto-committing on save, two people
# editing them independently means a guaranteed merge conflict where one person's rules
# silently replace the other's. They are personal working preferences, not build inputs —
# nothing in the site depends on them.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded, so both setups keep behaving the same without hand-syncing:
#   .claude/settings.json    — the graphify hook-guard config; static and rarely edited
#   .claude/skills/graphify/ — the graphify skill; installed by graphify itself, not npx skills
#   .agents/skills/          — the react-three-fiber skill pack; single tracked copy, see below
#
# To hand these rules to a collaborator, send them the standalone setup file rather than
# committing these back: novaiq-claude-setup.md, kept outside the repo.
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/CLAUDE.md

# .claude/skills/r3f-* were meant to be symlinks into .agents/skills/r3f-* (that's what
# `npx skills add` creates locally — one real copy, plus a Claude-Code-specific pointer to
# it), but git on Windows dereferenced them at commit time and checked in the full file
# content twice instead of a symlink. Two independently-committed copies of the same skill
# is exactly the shared-generated-directory problem graphify-out/ already ran into above:
# either of us reinstalling or updating the skill pack updates only one copy, and the stale
# other one becomes a guaranteed future conflict. .agents/skills/ stays tracked as the one
# real copy (portable, no symlink involved); each of us just runs
# `npx skills add EnzeD/r3f-skills` locally once to get our own correct local symlink at
# .claude/skills/r3f-* — that command is a no-op if .agents/skills/ already has the content
# from git, it only needs to (re)create the local pointer.
.claude/skills/r3f-*
.opencode

# Browser-automation scratch. The playwright-cli skill drops a page snapshot (and sometimes a
# full-page PNG) into here on every run — 49 of them, 1.5MB, were committed before this line
# existed. They are debugging output from one moment in one session and are never read again.
.playwright-cli/

# Build-analysis artifacts. `dist-eager-probe.js` and `dist-eager-meta.json` are regenerated by
# the bundler whenever the question comes up again; between them they were 10.6MB of git history
# describing a build that no longer exists.
dist-eager-*.js
dist-eager-*.json

# Chrome performance traces. Useful for an afternoon, 3.5MB forever.
Trace-*.json.gz
